.TH GETPW 3
.SH NAME
getpw \- get name from UID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "getpw(uid, buf)"
.B "char *buf;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B getpw
searches the password file for the (numerical)
.IR uid ,
and fills in
.I buf
with the corresponding line; it returns non-zero if
.I uid
could not be
found.
The line is null-terminated.
.SH FILES
/etc/passwd
.SH "SEE ALSO"
getpwent(3), passwd(4)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Non-zero return on error.
.sp
